{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1518205-destroying-non-relic-objects-in-shadowlands","id":1518205,"title":"Destroying non-relic objects in Shadowlands","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-17T15:19:23-07:00","id":1518205,"title":"Destroying non-relic objects in Shadowlands","content":"I have always believed that Shadowlands is the flip side of the Skinlands, and objects in Shadowlands are in the same locations as in the Skinlands. If an object <b>was destroyed</b> in the Skinlands but remains in the Shadowlands, it is a relic, which wraiths can claim and use in various ways. However, if something <b>still exists</b> in the Skinlands, wraiths can only accept its existence, right? A brick wall in the Skinlands is a brick wall in the Shadowlands (cracked and ugly due to Deathsight effects), and wraiths cannot move it. They must spend Corpus to pass through it, and the only way to remove the wall in the Shadowlands is to destroy it in the Skinlands using Arcanoi that can penetrate the Shroud, right?<br /> <br /> But then why does the Wraith Player's Guide (p.133) state that it is possible to dismantle buildings in the Shadowlands and such dismantling weakens the buildings in the Skinlands?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12954-adrax","name":"Adrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T18:07:38-07:00","id":1518208,"title":"","content":"Great question. I had forgotten this odd bit of text from the Player's Guide. I just reread it, and I'm confused. I have the same interpretation of the geography/metaphysics as you do, but the text you point out does not align with our idea. On that same page, there is a line that states that the Shadowlands are an almost exact &quot;copy&quot; of the Skinlands, which suggests that whoever wrote that text considers the Shadlowlands reflection of a still-extant Skinlands object to be something that can be destroyed independent of the Skinlands counterpart. The text even uses the word &quot;counterpart&quot;.<br /> <br /> All I can think is that the writer of that text views Shadowlands reflections differently than other Wraith writers. There's a conflict. Personally, I would ignore this text and fall back on my original idea that Shadowlands reflections cannot be messed with, but if the Skinlands object/building is destroyed, then it may cross over into being Relic material which can be manipulated by ghosts using normal means.<br /> <br /> I'd love someone out there to confirm or challenge this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-17T23:45:52-07:00","id":1518218,"title":"","content":"I think the idea here is that you can destroy or damage the 'soul' of an object, or maybe less abstract, the property that makes an object resonate with the emotions and memories of people. As the text goes on to say, people will care less about it, and it will deteriorate faster. I think of it as fast-forwarding the timeline of decay for the object, since it is effectively 'dead'. A brick wall would lose its integrity and start to crumble and overgrow, a machine would stop working properly. The object is still there in the Skinlands and reflected in the Shadowlands until it has decayed enough to cease existing in the former, and a Wraith still would have to spend Corpus to pass through it until that happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T04:36:56-07:00","id":1518235,"title":"","content":"To expand a little on the dual nature of things (how I see them): what the book calls Memoriam is the 'Shadowlands Body' of an object. It's the thing that has potential to become a Relic if it is strong enough, should the Skinlands object be destroyed - ie, the Skinlands Body is gone, Shadowlands Body remains. Destroying an object in the Shadowlands is the inversion of this: Shadowlands Body destroyed, Skinlands Body extant. It may be a bit tricky to visualize, but I think the analogy of soul and body helps. Both occupy the same space, are intimately linked, but are only tangible in their respective realms. I also think destruction of the Shadowlands Body is not irreversible.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> The owner of a car angers a Wraith, who proceeds to thrash the car with a soulsteel hammer in the Shadowlands. The hitherto reliable car develops rattles, hickups, equipment failure and generally starts to malfunction. The owner sells it to a car enthusiast who invests much love, work, and general passion into it. This would 'mend' the damage to the Memoriam, and it might even have a chance of becoming a relic should it be destroyed later on.<br /> <br /> The book tries to describe how the mix of Shadowlands and Skinlands presence can overlap with the earlier White House example. If you ever played a game where the level designer placed two instances of the same object by mistake, I imagine it like that. In the car example, one of the copies would be beaten up by an angry Wraith but still be attached to the Skinlands copy, and the damaged Shadowlands copy would be quite obvious to any other Wraith.<br /> <br /> The main difference to a Relic is that this Shadowlands copy doesn't really have a Corpus. It exists as a largely ephemeral thing, and the destruction process is more of a metaphysical process.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T04:57:25-07:00","id":1518236,"title":"","content":"To be fair Oblivion is the essence and source of entropy and death - it isn\u2019t the ultimate source of evil in the universe, but more a fundamental aspect of reality itself<br /> The Shadow is a fragment of Oblivion itself whispering inside the minds of the Wraiths<br /> Thus, I can totally immagine, by using this &quot;connection&quot;, a Wraith &quot;chanel&quot; the very power and essence of Entropy itself in to the said object and Oblivion simply &quot;devours&quot; it<br /> <br /> OR It is not unlike the connection between a Spirit, Material world and the Umbra of the Werewolf<br /> Te principal is the same, just the method is a bit different, but basically destroying the Memoriam you destroy/weaken the real thing itself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T11:19:51-07:00","id":1518260,"title":"","content":"I think the original poster's understanding is mostly correct. It's just that there is not the contradiction he thinks there is with that and the description in the Players Guide. Wraith just has a very strange non-Euclidean space that can be very confusing.<br /> <br /> For example, what happens when an important building with lots of emotional attachment burns down? It can become a relic building.<br /> <br /> But then what happens when a new building in the Skinlands goes up on that spot? Well, that building ends up having a presence in the Shadowlands as well.<br /> <br /> So we now have two buildings occupying the same space. That is impossible in the Skinlands. It is a normal thing in the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, Wraiths can build additional things in that spot as well. Hierarchy typically takes the most &quot;solid&quot; buildings in the Necropolis in the Shadowlands for use as a citadel. They improve that citadel with Stygian steel supports, soulforged bricks, salvaged relics, etc. so that 1) it can better withstand a maelstrom, and 2) make the normal kind of improvement any real estate developer does - turn the building into the kind of building they need. Besides adding materials, wraiths can therefore also remove them. If some wall is in the way, they cut it out and remove it (and likely repurpose it elsewhere) - doesn't matter if the material of that wall is Stygian steel, a relic body made of plasm, or the more ephemeral &quot;shadow&quot; of the Skinlands building.<br /> <br /> Skinland structures in the Shadowlands work according to the rule of ouch. And normally wraiths cannot affect them. But we do know there are Arcanoi that can. It's probably some variation of Inhabit - because that is the Arcanoi of the artificers - that allows them to remove/change/affect a Skinland's building/matter's &quot;shadow&quot; in the Shadowland. It mostly does not affect the actual building in the Skinlands, but it does do some sort of metaphysical damage that might manifest in some entropic way eventually in the Skinlands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T18:27:59-07:00","id":1518280,"title":"","content":"I'm still pretty confused, and I still see a contradiction between the metaphysics of Wraith compared to what we get in this passage. I'm aware of Arcanoi that affect Skinlands objects, and Arcanoi that affect Relics, but I still don't see how one can destroy only the &quot;soul&quot; or shadow reflection of a Skinlands building without destroying the Skinlands building itself.<br /> <br /> Even if a building is destroyed, becomes a relic, and a new version of the building is built in the same spot, you have two different things: one is a Skinlands building (and its reflection), the other is the Relic of the old building. The passage in question seems to be saying that you can destroy <i>just</i><i> the reflection</i> without destroying the skinlands material.<br /> <br /> Can someone point out an Arcanoi or official method for doing so? Inhabit and Flux, AFAIK, cannot do what the passage describes. They can affect Skinland objects directly, but I'm not aware of their being able to affect <i>only</i> the &quot;soul&quot; of those objects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T23:23:22-07:00","id":1518297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callishka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1518205-destroying-non-relic-objects-in-shadowlands?p=1518280#post1518280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone point out an Arcanoi or official method for doing so? Inhabit and Flux, AFAIK, cannot do what the passage describes. They can affect Skinland objects directly, but I'm not aware of their being able to affect <i>only</i> the &quot;soul&quot; of those objects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was assuming this simply happens when a Wraith applies 'physical' damage in the Shadowlands to an object <i>without</i> any special power. Like, punching it. But I can't think of a source for this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 07-19-2023, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T10:26:20-07:00","id":1518314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1518205-destroying-non-relic-objects-in-shadowlands?p=1518260#post1518260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just that there is not the contradiction</div> </div> </div> </div>But <b>there is</b> the contradiction! I know about Arcanoi that can affect an object in the Skinlands, thus affecting the same object in the Shadowlands as well. If an object doesn't exist in the Skinlands but exists in the Shadowlands, it is a relic, and there are Arcanoi that can affect relics. But what Arcanoi can affect an object in the Shadowlands without affecting it in the Skinlands?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12954-adrax","name":"Adrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T12:48:45-07:00","id":1518321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1518205-destroying-non-relic-objects-in-shadowlands?p=1518314#post1518314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what Arcanoi can affect an object in the Shadowlands without affecting it in the Skinlands?</div> </div> </div> </div>One we don't know about. This is not unusual for Wraith. When Wraith was first introduced, we were told Artificers - the users of Inhabit - made soulforged goods. Yet the actual Inhabit Arcanoi of the Artificers did not include any such rules for it. But it obviously existed. So it's not so much as a contradiction as a gap in the rules. RPG rules always have gaps because the mechanics are never meant to simulate the totality of reality. It just provides us mechanics for what they think are the most common needs for the game. GMs need to figure out other things for themselves.<br /> <br /> The setting is more than the mechanics of the game. That can be frustrating for players, but that is how it is.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T07:21:13-07:00","id":1518357,"title":"","content":"I understand that games will include things that the rules do not spell out how to do. I have no issue with that, and it does not frustrate me. What can be frustrating, however, is when the rulebook states something but does not make it clear that there are no supporting rules for how to do this. I don't like having to cast about from book to book looking for something that supports a passage, especially when it's on the fly, in the middle of a game. Now at least, thanks to this thread, I won't be alarmed by this passage if someone brings it up... I'll just know not to go looking for a rule, but to make up whatever fits my game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T07:28:14-07:00","id":1518358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1518205-destroying-non-relic-objects-in-shadowlands?p=1518297#post1518297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was assuming this simply happens when a Wraith applies 'physical' damage in the Shadowlands to an object <i>without</i> any special power. Like, punching it. But I can't think of a source for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>The setting is pretty clear that the only way for ghosts to do anything physical to Skinlands material is through Arcanoi such as outrage, embody, flux, or inhabit. Otherwise, you will either simply not affect the material, or you will force your fist straight through the object and do corpus damage to yourself. I would have appreciated if this passage contained something like:&quot;There exist secret methods for destroying The shadowlands reflection of an object...&quot;, just some text to signal to the readers that there is no point going through the book looking for the specific way of doing this, since it is not spelled out anywhere, Much the way they do when they talk about secret ways of lowering the shroud beyond a 4, or something like that, without actually providing rules for how to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T12:55:33-07:00","id":1518368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callishka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1518205-destroying-non-relic-objects-in-shadowlands?p=1518358#post1518358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The setting is pretty clear that the only way for ghosts to do anything physical to Skinlands material is through Arcanoi such as outrage, embody, flux, or inhabit. Otherwise, you will either simply not affect the material, or you will force your fist straight through the object and do corpus damage to yourself. I would have appreciated if this passage contained something like:&quot;There exist secret methods for destroying The shadowlands reflection of an object...&quot;, just some text to signal to the readers that there is no point going through the book looking for the specific way of doing this, since it is not spelled out anywhere, Much the way they do when they talk about secret ways of lowering the shroud beyond a 4, or something like that, without actually providing rules for how to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say it\u2019s either Shadowland variations of Outrage (to destroy) or inhabit (to manipulate or craft) memorium materials.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d rule that Soulsteel tools can replace Arcanoi as that means that regular workers can move or fortify walls etc (as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> said).<br /> <br /> In terms of official rules probably not going to happen with W20 outside of Storyteller Vault sourcebooks (which aren\u2019t canon but good nether the less).<br /> <br /> That said from a personal perspective as an ST it is good to have some latitude and flex unity to craft the setting .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T14:19:45-07:00","id":1518380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callishka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1518205-destroying-non-relic-objects-in-shadowlands?p=1518358#post1518358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The setting is pretty clear that the only way for ghosts to do anything physical to Skinlands material is through Arcanoi such as outrage, embody, flux, or inhabit. Otherwise, you will either simply not affect the material, or you will force your fist straight through the object and do corpus damage to yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, I think this may be where our interpretation diverges: I'm not saying that a Wraith punching an object would damage it in the Skinlands, it would damage its Memoriam in the Shadowlands. The damaged or destroyed Memoriam would then 'weaken' the object in the Skinlands, which I interpret as an increased rate of decay.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's easier to explain with a living object:<br /> Say a Sandman rips the soul out of a body, drags it into the nearest forge and has it made into an ashtray. The remaining body would biologically still function (ie, the Skinland 'object' appears undamaged) but would be little more than a husk, and probably not survive very long. Note the paragraph in the Player's Guide mentions &quot;the [destroyed] Memoriam of a building or person&quot;.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1518205-destroying-non-relic-objects-in-shadowlands?p=1518368#post1518368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d rule that Soulsteel tools can replace Arcanoi as that means that regular workers can move or fortify walls etc (as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> said).</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some indirect hints at this: Relics are basically hardened Memoriam and are fully interactable in the Shadowlands. Soulforging is a skill, not an Arcanos, which indicates that manipulation of Memoriam does not necessarily require an Art- but possibly an Artifact or other tool. I still think a Wraith putting a Soulsteel hammer to a car is enough to damage its Memoriam.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1518205-destroying-non-relic-objects-in-shadowlands?p=1518368#post1518368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d say it\u2019s either Shadowland variations of Outrage (to destroy) or inhabit (to manipulate or craft) memorium materials.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the Arcanos side, Flux has some Arts that increase the rate of decay of Skinlands object. While not stated as such, this may actually work by weakening the Memoriam of the object (since Flux has been reworked in Wr20 to deal with Relics and adjacent concepts). Outrage has Death's Touch, Tantrum, Wyldfire, and Obliviate which can all deal damage to Shadowland objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T01:38:12-07:00","id":1518419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callishka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1518205-destroying-non-relic-objects-in-shadowlands?p=1518280#post1518280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still pretty confused, and I still see a contradiction between the metaphysics of Wraith compared to what we get in this passage. I'm aware of Arcanoi that affect Skinlands objects, and Arcanoi that affect Relics, but I still don't see how one can destroy only the &quot;soul&quot; or shadow reflection of a Skinlands building without destroying the Skinlands building itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK, there is no specific method mentioned in Flux or Inhabit for this. However, the Pardoners possess an ability &quot;obliterate the soul&quot; which functions in a similar manner: it feeds the soul to Oblivion, while keeping the body alive but prone to decay. Doing the same for buildings with both Inhabit and Castigate (or Inhabit with added Angst) is very Wraith-like and begs for a role-played bargain with the Shadowguide, as it &quot;invites&quot; Oblivion into the shadow of a building, eradicating its presence in the Shadowlands and damning its counterpart in the Skinlands. In fact, I might even introduce such a building in my upcoming campaign, one that is invisible to wraiths in the Shadowlands (much to their horror), as it has been fully consumed by the Labyrinth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28102-stathmin","name":"Stathmin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T10:38:14-07:00","id":1518544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1518205-destroying-non-relic-objects-in-shadowlands?p=1518380#post1518380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are some indirect hints at this: Relics are basically hardened Memoriam and are fully interactable in the Shadowlands. Soulforging is a skill, not an Arcanos, which indicates that manipulation of Memoriam does not necessarily require an Art- but possibly an Artifact or other tool. I still think a Wraith putting a Soulsteel hammer to a car is enough to damage its Memoriam..</div> </div> </div> </div>This adds to the setting as well, Wraith differs from the other lines in that it\u2019s an entire realm populated by a large populations of aware wraiths, I like the idea of smaller settlements in both the Shadowlands and Dark Kingdoms where wraiths are just getting on with their afterlives and survive.<br /> <br /> I can imagine most wraiths would reconcile themselves to just eking out an existence, keep their heads down etc so being able to use Soulsteel tools would be key to this survival, plus breaking up and using memoria material would be essential for existence (if only to fortify Haunts) <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T13:06:34-07:00","id":1518561,"title":"","content":"I don't think non-Relic Memoriam can be used for any practical building, because it would completely destroy the Soulforging economy. If there was a viable alternative to Soulforging (same scenario if Shadowlands animals existed), it would be far less common.<br /> <br /> I look at it like this: Relics remain in the Shadowlands because they have active 'Fetters' to living persons. They are kind of the inverse of Wraith Fetter objects. Unfettered Memoriam would simply fade too fast to be of any practical use- nobody cares about a piece of drywall enough to keep it anchored in the Shadowlands. I don't even think it's enough to give it proper material presence in the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> You could of course rule that non-Relic Memoriam could be used for temporary fixing, but you would quickly run into a scenario where Wraiths would cannibalize everything around them, which would lead to a heavily deteriorated Skinlands areas in the long run - I'm thinking something like the abandoned areas in Detroit, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T13:36:53-07:00","id":1518565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1518205-destroying-non-relic-objects-in-shadowlands?p=1518561#post1518561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think non-Relic Memoriam can be used for any practical building, because it would completely destroy the Soulforging economy. If there was a viable alternative to Soulforging (same scenario if Shadowlands animals existed), it would be far less common.<br /> <br /> I look at it like this: Relics remain in the Shadowlands because they have active 'Fetters' to living persons. They are kind of the inverse of Wraith Fetter objects. Unfettered Memoriam would simply fade too fast to be of any practical use- nobody cares about a piece of drywall enough to keep it anchored in the Shadowlands. I don't even think it's enough to give it proper material presence in the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> You could of course rule that non-Relic Memoriam could be used for temporary fixing, but you would quickly run into a scenario where Wraiths would cannibalize everything around them, which would lead to a heavily deteriorated Skinlands areas in the long run - I'm thinking something like the abandoned areas in Detroit, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the temporary aspect of non-relic memoria could be a good hook, more as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> said moving walls etc<br /> <br /> However mechanically it does raise an interesting point which is that the memoria in some locales may be stronger than others, so a shiny new building might have really high resistance than an older decrepit building or one that\u2019s less significant in living memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T11:47:37-07:00","id":1518652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1518205-destroying-non-relic-objects-in-shadowlands?p=1518565#post1518565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so a shiny new building might have really high resistance than an older decrepit building or one that\u2019s less significant in living memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my humble opinion, it is quite the opposite<br /> A new, shiny building to the most is alien, with little connection, while an old, even decrepit building are &quot;stronger&quot;. It was there when you were a child, and will be there when you passed away, and deep down you know it<br /> It is like <i>Old Deuteronomy</i>\u200b<br /> <br /> &quot;At the sight of that placid and bland physiognomy<br /> When she sits in the sun on the vicarage wall<br /> Oldest inhabitant croaks<br /> Well, of all things, can it be really?<br /> Yes, no, oh, hi, oh my eye<br /> My mind may be wandering, but I confess<br /> I believe it is Old Deuteronomy&quot;<br /> <br /> Even if they don't pay attention, decades or even centuries worth of &quot;passive memory&quot; builds up in even an old, decrepit ruin<br /> It is part of the life, the scenery and the everyday routine to the point no one notices it...<br /> ...until it is gone<br /> But even after it is gone, demolished, people hard to forget it <i>was there</i>, and in most minds it is <i>still there</i><br /> I think, and of course this is just my two cents, the shiny new\u200b buildings are the ones wiht the less significance in living memory","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T14:44:54-07:00","id":1518663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1518205-destroying-non-relic-objects-in-shadowlands?p=1518652#post1518652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my humble opinion, it is quite the opposite<br /> A new, shiny building to the most is alien, with little connection, while an old, even decrepit building are &quot;stronger&quot;. It was there when you were a child, and will be there when you passed away, and deep down you know it<br /> It is like <i>Old Deuteronomy</i>\u200b<br /> <br /> &quot;At the sight of that placid and bland physiognomy<br /> When she sits in the sun on the vicarage wall<br /> Oldest inhabitant croaks<br /> Well, of all things, can it be really?<br /> Yes, no, oh, hi, oh my eye<br /> My mind may be wandering, but I confess<br /> I believe it is Old Deuteronomy&quot;<br /> <br /> Even if they don't pay attention, decades or even centuries worth of &quot;passive memory&quot; builds up in even an old, decrepit ruin<br /> It is part of the life, the scenery and the everyday routine to the point no one notices it...<br /> ...until it is gone<br /> But even after it is gone, demolished, people hard to forget it <i>was there</i>, and in most minds it is <i>still there</i><br /> I think, and of course this is just my two cents, the shiny new\u200b buildings are the ones wiht the less significance in living memory</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see your point I think the distinction I\u2019m trying to make is that newer modern buildings might be harder to damage but less likely to manifest as memoria.<br /> <br /> Perhaps they are fainter than memoria buildings so moving walls etc are harder due to their intangibility.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T23:36:42-07:00","id":1518684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1518205-destroying-non-relic-objects-in-shadowlands?p=1518663#post1518663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see your point I think the distinction I\u2019m trying to make is that newer modern buildings might be harder to damage but less likely to manifest as memoria.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I see, sorry, misunderstood you<br /> It could be debatable tho', at least in my opinion; those old buildings were made quite durable and alreay stand the test of time, while the glass and steel towers are more &quot;fragile&quot; than the age old stone with more weak points to exploits<br /> Of course destroy the foundation and eventually everything will colapse <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Individual parts are down to personal taste so to speak, a steal door could be stronger than a wooden one, but then you &quot;attack&quot; the door frame and the hinges not the door itself (or the technologycal lock ), but a new concrate wall will be harder to eaten away by Oblivion thats for sure than an older thing<br /> <br /> So yeah, you are right <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T15:59:49-07:00","id":1518724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1518205-destroying-non-relic-objects-in-shadowlands?p=1518380#post1518380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh, I think this may be where our interpretation diverges: I'm not saying that a Wraith punching an object would damage it in the Skinlands, it would damage its Memoriam in the Shadowlands. The damaged or destroyed Memoriam would then 'weaken' the object in the Skinlands, which I interpret as an increased rate of decay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting ideas here, but you're correct in thinking that our interpretation diverges on this point. I do not read &quot;Memoriam&quot; how you do; Memoriam is repeatedly and clearly described as being about how the living feel about dead people, the emotion the living continue to funnel into the memory of the deceased. &quot;Infamy&quot; is the flip side, and is described as such: the energy of fear, loathing, etc, that the living feel for a dead person's memory. Memoriam is also closely linked to pathos, since it represents the emotional energy invested into someone who has passed away and is tapped as a fuel source by ghosts.<br /> <br /> I do not associate Memoriam with Relics, which while they do involve emotions and memory as well (as does everything in this setting), are described without reference to memoriam.<br /> <br /> I don't really get what it would mean to damage the emotional energy invested into an object or structure by striking it physically, especially since many objects and structures do not provide any Pathos (and thus are not assigned a Memoriam rating). Are we saying that even objects without Memoriam have some trace amount of it which cannot be tapped for Pathos but which can be damaged physically?<br /> <br /> Now I can't remember whether, besides this passage, the setting ever talks about there even being such thing as the &quot;soul&quot; or Shadowlands reflection of a living object. Isn't there only the skinland objects, how they appear through the shroud, and relic material? Basically, I'm not sure that any other part of the setting backs up the model being suggested in this passage. As far as I remember, from the point of view of a ghost, a Skinlands structure exists <i>over there</i>, on the other side of the Shroud, not here with us. There aren't two copies, one living and one destroyed, superimosed; there is only the living one. There isn't a soul in it for us to manipulate. The structure only crosses over into our reach when it is destroyed or lost forever.<br /> <br /> I could be wrong on this, and I would sincerely love to see a passage that backs up what we see in this passage.<br /> <br /> For clarity: Any gaming group can do whatever they want with the setting and interpret it however they like--I just like knowing where the written-rules end and my opinion begins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","user":"Callishka","date":". 07-24-2023, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}